Z||000000||artherd||08-31-2001||02:49 AM||||Guess what I ran into when I finally droped the cradle on the donor car for the N* swap?   Yep, driver's side rear cradle bolt SPUN in the frame.    Cut hole in frame on the side, grab the da*& thing, pull bolt the rest of the way off (after heating it with acytelene torch, then shoving a candle in there to loosten with wax) and finally pulled bolt out.<P>Phew.<P>So now I've gotta fix this mess, and the weak-arse sheatmetal that was holding the nut from turning is just about gone. <P>I think I will end up fabing something to do the same job (hold, loosely, the whole assembley from turning. loseness is present to allow some ajustability/fit when putting in new cradles.<P>I just thought I'd Bitc* about it a bit. darned things!!  I'm now thingking, do I open up the other (aparently fine, aparently unrested) side?<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
