Z||000003||artherd||08-31-2001||07:03 PM||||Hi Joe, the first (read: this one) N* swap will be into my Silver hardtop formula (sunroof  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  as this car currently has, nay, HAD! a blown engine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I'm doing the 'project' rougher car first, then when I get all the bugs out of the swap and it's running nicely and really fast, I plan to put a brand new crate northstar into the (70kmiles, garaged) T-top!<P>This is of course all assuming I win the lottery, at my present income rate, it is going to take some time for me to finish the silver car (just pulled the getrag off the old motor and cleaned and painted it today, now it's clean enough for the garage, heh. Time to replace some seals and mod for the N*'s starter and that kind of thing.<P>Still need to find Keith Huff and pick his brain about the Quartermaster clutch.  I like the theroy of it.  <P>Lots to do yet, but it's coming!!!<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KissMySSFiero:<BR><B>are you putting the Nstar in your ttop car or another?  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
